    <string name="onb1_title">Less scrolling, nothing given up</string>
    <string name="onb1_text">When you open short videos, a screen asks whether you really want to stay. Messages and regular videos keep working.</string>
    <string name="onb2_title">One permission needed</string>
    <string name="onb2_text">To notice that you are in Reels, the app has to read the structure of the screen. It does not read your messages, saves nothing and has no internet access. Android will show a warning: it is the same for every app that uses this permission.</string>
    <string name="onb2_restricted">If the switch is greyed out or you see \"Restricted setting\": open Settings › Apps › Reels Killer, tap the three dots at the top right and choose \"Allow restricted settings\". Then come back here.</string>
